## Objectives

The primary goal of GUTS IAM is to make access control simple, secure, and not a chaotic mess of hardcoded permissions and forgotten rules.

The system is designed to ensure that every user, service, and request is properly authenticated and authorized before touching any sensitive resources.

Key objectives include:

- Centralize identity and access management so everything is controlled from one place instead of scattered logic everywhere
- Provide secure authentication to ensure only valid users get in (no freeloaders allowed)
- Enforce role-based authorization so access is structured and predictable, not random
- Reduce manual access handling and administrative overhead
- Improve system security by enforcing consistent access policies
- Maintain accountability through traceable and auditable actions
- Support scalable access control as the system grows beyond “just a small project” stage
